@@ -0,0 +1,283 @@
+# Workflow: STEP Computational-Geometry Analysis
+
+Parse a STEP file into computational-geometry evidence and local visual
+artifacts, without reconstructing an editable model.
+
+## 1. Scope
+
+Use this workflow when the user asks to parse a STEP, identify all supported
+geometric feature candidates, create feature highlights and planar section
+views, or produce a local analysis artifact package.
+
+Do not use it for a single read-only question about a dimension, entity, or
+topology fact; use `references/domains/step-inspection.md` directly. Do not use
+it when the deliverable is an editable model, candidate STEP, or modeling
+commands; use `references/workflows/step-reconstruction.md`.
+
+Every reported feature remains a `geometric_candidate`. It is evidence about
+the final BREP, not recovered feature history, a unique command order,
+manufacturing intent, or a process conclusion.
+
+## 2. Non-negotiable boundaries
+
+- Treat the target STEP and its directory as read-only.
+- Require a user-specified absolute output directory isolated from the target
+  directory; do not invent an output location.
+- Run inspection only outside `GraphSession`.
+- Bind every report, index, image record, section record, and manifest entry to
+  the same target STEP SHA-256.
+- Use one saved authoritative manufacturing-hint report for candidate entity
+  IDs and parameters. Per-candidate images and section planning consume that
+  report rather than rerunning candidate recognition.
+- Stop after the analysis package is complete.
+
+**Explicit terminal boundary:** this workflow must not build a candidate
+model or candidate STEP, create model JSON or an operation sequence, run a
+model audit or strict replay, perform STEP roundtrip or target/candidate
+comparison, or enter reconstruction iteration.
+
+## 3. Inputs
+
+- absolute path to one `.step` or `.stp` target;
+- absolute output directory;
+- requested feature kinds, defaulting explicitly to the complete currently
+  supported set:
+
+  ```python
+  feature_kinds = ("fillet", "chamfer", "sheet_metal", "hole", "extrusion")
+  ```
+
+- optional recorded linear tolerance, angular tolerance, and `max_hints`;
+- optional user-specified section planes; otherwise use the deterministic
+  planning rules in Phase 5.
+
+Unspecified values must be recorded explicitly in `analysis-config.json`
+before inspection. They may not remain hidden runtime defaults.
+
+## 4. Required reading and API pages
+
+Before inspecting the target, read these completely:
+
+- `references/inspect/brep-reverse-engineering.md`;
+- `references/domains/step-inspection.md`.
+
+Before the first call, read the exact page for every selected API:
+
+- `references/docs/api/inspect_step_rsummary.md`;
+- `references/docs/api/inspect_manufacturing_hints_rdescriptor.md`;
+- `references/docs/api/render_manufacturing_hints_rpath.md`;
+- `references/docs/api/render_region_rpath.md`;
+- `references/docs/api/inspect_section_rdescriptor.md`;
+- `references/docs/api/render_sections_rpath.md`.
+
+## 5. Workflow
+
+Execute phases serially. A later phase cannot pass until the prior phase has
+produced its named artifacts and passed its gate. On failure, write
+`run-status.json` with status `failed`, the failed phase, and a bounded error
+summary before stopping.
+
+### Phase 1: Freeze input and run parameters
+
+Validate that the target exists and has a `.step` or `.stp` suffix. Compute its
+SHA-256, verify that the output directory is isolated from the target
+directory, and record SDK version, timestamp, platform, explicit
+`feature_kinds`, tolerances, `max_hints`, and section-plane rules.
+
+Write:
+
+- `analysis-config.json`;
+- `requirement-brief.md`.
+
+**Gate:** the absolute input/output paths, target hash, units, and every runtime
+parameter exist on disk. Do not continue with an unrecorded default.
+
+### Phase 2: Build the BREP index and global summary
+
+Call `inspect_step_rsummary` with keyword arguments and write
+`target-summary.json`. Include bounds, area, volume, centroid, entity counts,
+surface statistics, and units. Enable `include_parameter_groups=True` at most
+once, and only when radii, angles, or repeated carrier groups are needed.
+
+**Gate:** the STEP is readable, its BREP index succeeds, and the summary
+contains units and entity counts. A read failure stops the workflow; never
+degrade to screenshot-only analysis.
+
+### Phase 3: Run and validate authoritative feature recognition
+
+Run `inspect_manufacturing_hints_rdescriptor` once with all requested kinds
+explicitly supplied:
+
+```python
+hints = brep.inspect_manufacturing_hints_rdescriptor(
+    model_or_path=target_model,
+    feature_kinds=("fillet", "chamfer", "sheet_metal", "hole", "extrusion"),
+    tolerance=linear_tolerance,
+    angular_tolerance_degrees=angular_tolerance_degrees,
+    max_hints=max_hints,
+)
+```
+
+Write the unchanged descriptor to `manufacturing-hints.json` and a normalized
+candidate lookup to `feature-index.json`. Record diagnostics and regions that
+did not form strong candidates in `unresolved-features.md`.
+
+**Gate:** `truncated` is `false`. When it is `true`, increase `max_hints` and
+rerun the one authoritative analysis in full; a truncated report is not a
+complete parse. Every candidate's `body_id`, `entity_ids`, and
+`highlight_entity_ids` must resolve in the same unchanged BREP index, and each
+candidate must retain geometric parameters, evidence, and a confidence
+explanation. Zero candidates is valid: preserve the empty report and
+diagnostics and state that no supported feature was identified.
+
+### Phase 4: Render feature highlights
+
+For a non-empty authoritative report:
+
+1. Call `render_manufacturing_hints_rpath` with the same explicit feature set,
+   tolerances, and effective `max_hints`; write
+   `highlights/all-features.png`.
+2. For every highlightable candidate, call `render_region_rpath` with the
+   saved `highlight_entity_ids`; write
+   `highlights/<candidate-kind>/<safe-hint-id>.png`.
+
+Replace Windows-forbidden filename characters with `_` without changing the
+original `hint_id` in reports. For example,
+`hole_region_candidate:0` becomes `hole_region_candidate_0.png`.
+
+Write `highlight-index.json` with `hint_id`, candidate kind, stable category
+color, entity IDs, image-relative path, and target SHA-256. Every view keeps a
+distinguishable opaque base model. If there are zero candidates, do not call a
+renderer that requires highlighted faces; record `not_applicable` in the
+index.
+
+**Gate:** every highlightable candidate has exactly one per-candidate image;
+the overview exists when applicable. Images are human-review evidence and do
+not replace Phase 3 candidate validation.
+
+### Phase 5: Plan deterministic section planes
+
+Write every plane to `section-plan.json` with `section_id`, source, associated
+`hint_id` values, origin, unit normal, purpose, and generation rule. Apply
+these priorities:
+
+1. User-specified planes.
+2. For each hole, one transverse plane through the axis midpoint with normal
+   equal to the hole axis, plus one longitudinal plane containing the axis.
+   Determine the longitudinal normal by crossing the hole axis with the global
+   axis least parallel to it.
+3. For each extrusion, transverse planes at 25%, 50%, and 75% between start and
+   end faces, normal to the extrusion direction.
+4. For other candidates, use the merged `highlight_entity_ids` bounding-box
+   center and the global axis for its smallest extent, unless evidence supplies
+   a more specific support-face normal.
+5. Always add XY, XZ, and YZ planes through the model bounding-box center so a
+   zero-candidate run still has viewable sections.
+
+Planes are duplicates when origins differ by no more than the recorded linear
+tolerance and normals are parallel or antiparallel within the recorded angular
+tolerance. Keep the higher-priority plane and attach every related candidate
+to its index entry.
+
+**Gate:** every normal is finite, non-zero, and normalized; every automatic
+plane traces to candidate parameters, selected-entity bounds, or model bounds.
+Never guess a plane from a screenshot.
+
+### Phase 6: Compute and render 2D sections
+
+For each planned plane, call `inspect_section_rdescriptor` with
+`compact=False` so every contour keeps `samples_2d`. Write one complete result
+to `sections/data/<section-id>.json`. Then call `render_sections_rpath` once
+with those saved descriptors in plan order and write
+`sections/section-atlas.png`.
+
+Use titles containing `section_id`, source, associated candidates, and
+material area. Preserve local X/Y millimetre coordinates and equal aspect.
+Material outer contours, holes, nested material, and open contours must remain
+visually distinct. Write `section-index.json` with a one-to-one panel/data
+mapping and target SHA-256.
+
+An empty section produces an explicit panel showing its plane metadata. A
+compact descriptor or a contour without `samples_2d` is an error; regenerate
+the detailed section instead of silently omitting it.
+
+**Gate:** every planned plane has one data JSON and one atlas panel, in the
+same deterministic order.
+
+### Phase 7: Report, manifest, and stop
+
+Write `parse-report.md` containing the target summary, candidate counts by
+kind, each candidate's main geometric parameters and evidence summary, links
+to its highlight, links to section data/atlas, limitations, and unresolved
+items. Write `artifact-manifest.json` with each artifact's relative path,
+role, byte size, SHA-256, and target SHA-256. Finally write `run-status.json`
+with status `complete`.
+
+**Gate:** all required evidence, indexes, images, reports, and manifests exist;
+all records bind the same target SHA-256; the output tree contains no artifact
+from the explicitly forbidden reconstruction stages. End the workflow here.
+
+## 6. Failure routes
+
+| Failure | Required response |
+| --- | --- |
+| Target missing, invalid suffix, or unreadable BREP | Write failed Phase 1/2 status and stop; do not use screenshots as a substitute |
+| Output directory overlaps the target directory | Ask for an isolated absolute output directory and stop |
+| Authoritative report is truncated | Increase `max_hints`, replace the incomplete authoritative report, and rerun dependent phases |
+| Candidate IDs do not resolve in the same BREP index | Mark the report invalid and rerun against the unchanged indexed target |
+| No supported candidate exists | Preserve empty report/diagnostics and continue with global sections |
+| A per-candidate render fails | Record the candidate and error; do not claim a complete run |
+| Plane evidence is insufficient or normal is invalid | Record the unresolved item; do not guess from a render |
+| Section is compact or lacks `samples_2d` | Recompute that detailed section with `compact=False` |
+| Atlas or manifest is incomplete | Write failed status; do not enter any reconstruction phase |
+
+## 7. Deliverables
+
+```text
+<absolute-output-directory>/
+  requirement-brief.md
+  analysis-config.json
+  target-summary.json
+  manufacturing-hints.json
+  feature-index.json
+  highlight-index.json
+  section-plan.json
+  section-index.json
+  parse-report.md
+  unresolved-features.md
+  run-status.json
+  artifact-manifest.json
+  highlights/
+    all-features.png
+    <candidate-kind>/
+      <safe-hint-id>.png
+  sections/
+    section-atlas.png
+    data/
+      <section-id>.json
+```
+
+`highlights/all-features.png` is absent only for a zero-candidate run whose
+`highlight-index.json` says `not_applicable`.
+
+Forbidden deliverables include `*.model.json`, any candidate STEP,
+`operation-sequence.json` or other operation sequence, `model-audit.json` or
+other model audit, `strict-replay-report.json` or other strict replay output,
+any roundtrip report, target/candidate comparison images or reports, and any
+reconstruction iteration log.
+
+## 8. Completion gate
+
+A run is complete only when:
+
+- configuration, brief, global summary, authoritative hints, parse report,
+  indexes, run status, and manifest exist;
+- every non-zero candidate has its per-candidate highlight;
+- every planned plane has section data and an atlas panel;
+- every artifact and index binds the same target SHA-256;
+- `run-status.json` is `complete`;
+- no forbidden reconstruction artifact was generated.
+
+The completion verdict is an analysis-package verdict only. It does not claim
+recovered design intent, manufacturing process, editable reconstruction, or
+BREP equivalence to a separately built model.
